WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:07.960
The immediate effects of the UBI are
twofold.

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:13.870
The first is that involuntary poverty
will be ended. By involuntary poverty I

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:19.210
mean people who are trying real hard,
doing the best they can but cannot make

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:24.220
enough money to live a decent existence.
That kind of poverty goes away with the

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:29.770
passage of a universal basic income. A
second thing that the UBI does is it

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.770
utterly changes the incentives facing
people.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:38.050
It completely changes the incentives
that a woman faces in deciding whether

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.039
to have a baby,

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:43.989
for example. Other things such as
retirement for the elderly become much

00:00:43.989 --> 00:00:46.390
simpler with the universal basic income.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:50.620
Guess what? Social Security doesn't cover
everybody. We have lots of elderly in

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:55.659
poverty. That doesn't happen under a
universal basic income. In that in many

00:00:55.659 --> 00:01:01.479
other ways, we are looking at a system in
which problems that have been unsolvable

00:01:01.479 --> 00:01:06.100
by the welfare state are solved pretty
much as soon as the bill is passed.

